  {
    "speaker": "sheldon_cooper",
    "start": 33.60000000000002,
    "end": 46.809999999999945,
    "text": "You're holding two moderate spell cards, a small rock and a potion of Zancor, which will be about as much help as an air conditioner on the ice planet Hoth. Your only move is to play the potion, lose the skirmish, and two moves later, the game."
  },
  {
    "speaker": "wil_wheaton",
    "start": 48.69999999999993,
    "end": 49.41999999999996,
    "text": "I think he's got me."
  },
  {
    "speaker": "sheldon_cooper",
    "start": 49.69999999999993,
    "end": 78.54000000000008,
    "text": "The year was 1995, the place, Jackson, Mississippi. Having spent ten hours on a bus, during which I had to twice violate my personal rule against relieving myself on board a moving vehicle, I finally arrived at the fourth annual Dixie-Trek convention only to find that my idol Wil Wheaton decided he had better things to do than to show up and sign my action figure."
  }
